NAME
    read-key - read and normalize one key from the controlling terminal

SYNOPSIS
    read-key

DESCRIPTION
    read-key is a standalone POSIX-shell terminal utility. It reads one key from
    /dev/tty in non-canonical no-echo mode and restores terminal state before
    returning.

    Recognized terminal keys are written as symbolic names, including arrows,
    Home, End, Insert, Delete, PageUp/PageDown, function keys f1 through f20,
    Enter, Backspace, Tab, Backtab, Escape and NUL.

    Printable ASCII and one valid UTF-8 character are returned as themselves.
    Terminal-specific key sequences are obtained from terminfo when available.

EXIT STATUS
    0   A supported key or character was read.
    1   Controlling-terminal, terminfo or I/O/setup failure.
    2   Invalid invocation or unsupported/invalid/incomplete input.
